## 2026-03-19: Styling stack — BaseUI + CSS Modules
Tailwind CSS and shadcn/ui are not used. The UI stack is Base UI (unstyled accessible primitives) + CSS Modules for all styling. CSS Module files are named `ComponentName.module.css` and co-located with their component. Inline style objects are only acceptable for dynamic computed values.

## 2026-03-19: DES:: epic prefix for Design work
Added `DES::` as a new Jira epic team prefix for Design epics (mockups, UX review, design system work). Distinct from `DE::` which means Desktop/Tauri/Rust. The full epic prefix set is now: BE, FE, DE, DES, INF.

## 2026-03-19: .cursor/rules/ as the single convention source
`.cursor/rules/*.mdc` is the single source of truth for all conventions — shared by both Cursor and Claude Code. `.claude/CLAUDE.md` is a pointer file that directs Claude Code to read the `.cursor/rules/` files. No conventions are duplicated across the two locations.

## 2026-05-04: Full stack definition — CF-native, TanStack Start, server-authoritative offline

**Stack — locked:**

| Layer | Choice |
|---|---|
| Web framework | TanStack Start (SSR for web, SPA mode for desktop) |
| Desktop shell | Tauri 2.0 — wraps TanStack Start SPA build. No separate React app in apps/desktop/. |
| Mobile | Expo / React Native (future) |
| API | Hono on Cloudflare Workers — same Worker as TanStack Start, mounted at /api/$ |
| Database | Neon (Postgres) |
| ORM | Drizzle + drizzle-zod |
| Connection pooling | Cloudflare Hyperdrive |
| Auth | Better Auth |
| Tenant isolation | Postgres RLS (set via session context in transaction wrapper) |
| Client state | TanStack Query — structured to migrate to TanStack DB when v1 ships |
| Offline | Server-authoritative + optimistic updates + durable SQLite mutation queue |
| Offline SQLite | wa-sqlite/OPFS (web), native Tauri SQL plugin (desktop), expo-sqlite (mobile) |
| Source sync | Cloudflare Queues (webhook ingest) + CF Cron Triggers (Jira polling fallback) |
| Real-time | Deferred post-v1 — CF Durable Objects + WebSocket |
| Type flow | Drizzle schema → drizzle-zod → Hono RPC → hc typed client → component props |

**Build targets — one TanStack Start codebase, two outputs:**
- `BUILD_TARGET=web` → SSR output, deploys to CF Workers
- `BUILD_TARGET=desktop` → SPA mode (`spa: { enabled: true }`), outputs static `dist/`, Tauri packages it
- Server functions in SPA mode automatically become HTTP calls to the Hono API — no code changes required

**Tauri architecture:**
- `apps/desktop/` is Rust shell only — Tauri config, native plugins, no React
- Main window loads TanStack Start SPA at `/`
- Tray window is a second Tauri window loading the same SPA at `/tray` — one binary, two windows
- Both windows share one native SQLite database via Tauri SQL plugin
- Main window owns the mutation queue drainer; tray window is a reader/writer only
- Hono API must allow `tauri://localhost` as a CORS origin

**Monorepo structure:**
```
apps/
  web/          TanStack Start (SSR for web, SPA for Tauri)
  desktop/      Tauri shell only (Rust, tauri.conf.json, native plugins)
  mobile/       Expo (future)
  api/          Hono on CF Workers
packages/
  ui/           Shared React components
  api-client/   Typed Hono hc client — used by web, desktop, mobile
  queue/        Mutation queue abstraction — pure TS, platform-agnostic drivers
  db/           Drizzle schema + drizzle-zod types — imported by api/ only
```

**Offline mutation queue:**
1. User action → serializable command with client UUID (idempotency key)
2. Optimistic update applied to TanStack Query cache immediately
3. Command persisted to SQLite queue (survives app kills)
4. Background drainer sends commands to Hono API FIFO with exponential backoff
5. Server applies RLS + business rules + optimistic concurrency, returns canonical state
6. Server `processed_mutations` table enables safe idempotent retries
7. Conflicts: 409 version / 422 business rule / 403 permission → rollback + rejected-mutation UI

**Source integration:**
- Sync boundary: Jira Board (within Space), Linear Team, GitHub Repository
- Status mapping defined at connection time — display always uses source vocabulary
- Webhook ingest → CF Queue → consumer Worker → Neon
- CF Cron Trigger polls Jira periodically (Jira webhooks are best-effort, no replay)

**Core data model:**
```
Spec (synced from source)
  └── Action (Stride-native, 1+ per Spec)
        └── Session (Stride-native, time block on an Action)

Standalone Action (no parent Spec — personal tasks, title + estimate only)
  └── Session
```
Execution always ties to an Action. Sessions never attach directly to a Spec.

**Explicitly rejected — do not reintroduce without a new decision entry:**
- PowerSync (RLS gap on client-side SQLite)
- Supabase (ecosystem lock-in)
- TanStack DB in production now (persistence alpha as of 0.6)
- ElectricSQL as primary sync layer
- Separate TanStack Start app for Tauri (one codebase, two build outputs)
- Tray as a separate Tauri binary (one binary, two windows)
- Stride-native Specs (all Specs have a source system; standalone tasks use Actions)
- Sessions tied directly to Specs (must go through an Action)
